IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa25-records.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 37 "Companies: supplementary provisions",
-- Company records: ss 1134 to 1138 (lines 16190-16251 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result").
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes, or (for a "has complied" function) every requirement that engages is met.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words. Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide. Each such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>), <why> being one of:
--               silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the text, limited by its own wording.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Answers other parts or the keel give are INPUTS under the names PLAN.md section 4 gives them
-- (`s 1121 the officer is in default`, `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts`).
-- Every name below begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- Company records (ss 1134 to 1138)
-- =========================================================================================================

§ `Part 37: companies, supplementary provisions`

§§ `Company records`

-- ---- s 1134: Meaning of "company records" --------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16192 | 1134 Meaning of “company records”
-- src:16193 | In this Part “company records” means—
-- src:16194 | (a) any register, index, accounting records, agreement, memorandum, minutes or other document required by the Companies Acts to be kept by a company, and
-- src:16195 | (b) any register kept by a company of its debenture holders.
@ref s 1134 Meaning of "company records" (src:16192-16195)
GIVEN `a provision of the Companies Acts requires the document to be kept by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the document is a register kept by a company of its debenture holders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1134 the document is a company record` MEANS
    IF `the document is a register kept by a company of its debenture holders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `a provision of the Companies Acts requires the document to be kept by a company`
         THEN CONSIDER `s 2(1) the provision is one of the Companies Acts`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“company records” means— (a) any register, index, accounting records, agreement, memorandum, minutes or other document required by the Companies Acts to be kept by a company"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the requiring provision is one of the Companies Acts is the answer of s 2(1)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part “company records” means— (a) any register, index, accounting records, agreement, memorandum, minutes or other document required by the Companies Acts to be kept by a company, and (b) any register kept by a company of its debenture holders"

-- ---- s 1135: Form of company records ---------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:16196 | 1135 Form of company records
-- src:16197 | (1) Company records—
-- src:16198 | (a) may be kept in hard copy or electronic form, and
-- src:16199 | (b) may be arranged in such manner as the directors of the company think fit,
-- src:16200 | provided the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference.
@ref s 1135(1) Form of company records (src:16196-16200)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
      `the records are arranged in the manner the directors of the company think fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1135(1) the company may keep its records in this way` MEANS
    IF NOT `the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference"
    ELSE CONSIDER form
         WHEN `hard copy form` THEN -- (a) "may be kept in hard copy or electronic form"
              IF `the records are arranged in the manner the directors of the company think fit`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) may be arranged in such manner as the directors of the company think fit"
         WHEN `electronic form` THEN
              IF `the records are arranged in the manner the directors of the company think fit`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) may be arranged in such manner as the directors of the company think fit"

-- src:16201 | (2) Where the records are kept in electronic form, they must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form.
@ref s 1135(2) Electronic records must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form (src:16201)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1135(2) the requirement of reproduction in hard copy form applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `electronic form` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the records are kept in electronic form" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16201 | (2) Where the records are kept in electronic form, they must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form.
@ref s 1135(2) Electronic records must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form (src:16201)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
      `the electronic records are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1135(2) the company has met the requirement of reproduction in hard copy form` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `hard copy form` THEN JUST TRUE -- the requirement does not engage: nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    WHEN `electronic form` THEN
        IF `the electronic records are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- Whether the company has complied with s 1135 as a whole: the proviso of (1) and the requirement of (2).
-- src:16196 | 1135 Form of company records
-- src:16197 | (1) Company records—
-- src:16198 | (a) may be kept in hard copy or electronic form, and
-- src:16199 | (b) may be arranged in such manner as the directors of the company think fit,
-- src:16200 | provided the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference.
-- src:16201 | (2) Where the records are kept in electronic form, they must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form.
@ref s 1135 Form of company records (the whole section, for the offence in subsection (3)) (src:16196-16201)
GIVEN form IS A `Form of document`
      `the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the electronic records are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1135 the company has complied with this section` MEANS
    IF NOT `the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "provided the information in question is adequately recorded for future reference"
    ELSE `s 1135(2) the company has met the requirement of reproduction in hard copy form` form `the electronic records are capable of being reproduced in hard copy form`

-- src:16202 | (3) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1135(3) Offence of failing to comply with s 1135 (src:16202)
GIVEN `s 1135 the company has complied with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1135(3) an officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1135 the company has complied with this section`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed" (an "if" that is not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company complied is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121

-- src:16203 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1135(4) Penalty for an offence under s 1135 (src:16203)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1135(4) the penalty for an offence under s 1135` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- The pounds a fine limit stands for. The Act does not say what a level on the standard scale or the statutory
-- maximum is worth: both are INPUTS (Guide section 4), never a number from memory. Used by the seat layer.
GIVEN limit IS A `Fine limit`
      `the pounds that the level on the standard scale stands for` IS A NUMBER
      `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1135(4) the fine limit in pounds` MEANS
    CONSIDER limit
    WHEN `a fine without a stated limit` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no limit is stated
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that the statutory maximum stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` level fraction THEN JUST (fraction TIMES `the pounds that the level on the standard scale stands for`)
    WHEN `a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` pounds THEN JUST pounds

-- src:16204 | (5) Any provision of an instrument made by a company before 12th February 1979 that requires a register of holders of the company's debentures to be kept in hard copy form is to be read as requiring it to be kept in hard copy or electronic form.
@ref s 1135(5) Instruments made before 12th February 1979 requiring a hard copy register of debenture holders (src:16204)
GIVEN `the date the instrument was made` IS A DATE
      `the instrument requires a register of holders of the company's debentures to be kept in hard copy form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1135(5) the instrument's requirement is to be read as requiring hard copy or electronic form` MEANS
    IF `the instrument requires a register of holders of the company's debentures to be kept in hard copy form`
       AND `the date the instrument was made` LESS THAN (Date 12 2 1979)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any provision of an instrument made by a company before 12th February 1979 that requires a register of holders of the company's debentures to be kept in hard copy form"

-- ---- s 1136: Regulations about where certain company records are kept available for inspection -----------
-- s 1136(1), (3), (4), (5) and (7) are a regulation-making power and its procedure: inert, reason 2 (NOTES.md).
-- The list of "relevant provisions" in subsection (2) is a defined term and is encoded. Five entries of the list
-- are shown as dots in the text (lines 16209, 16210, 16213, 16218, 16219): they are blank rows.

-- src:16207 | (2) The “relevant provisions” are—
-- src:16208 | section 114 (register of members);
-- src:16211 | section 228 (directors' service contracts);
-- src:16212 | section 237 (directors' indemnities);
-- src:16214 | section 358 (records of resolutions etc);
-- src:16215 | section 702 (contracts relating to purchase of own shares);
-- src:16216 | section 720 (documents relating to redemption or purchase of own shares out of capital by private company);
-- src:16217 | section 743 (register of debenture holders);
-- src:16220 | section 805 (report to members of outcome of investigation by public company into interests in its shares);
-- src:16221 | section 809 (register of interests in shares disclosed to public company);
-- src:16222 | section 859Q (instruments creating charges).
@ref s 1136(2) The "relevant provisions" (src:16207-16222)
GIVEN `the number of the section of the Companies Act 2006` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1136(2) the provision is a relevant provision` MEANS
    IF elem `the number of the section of the Companies Act 2006`
            (LIST "114", "228", "237", "358", "702", "720", "743", "805", "809", "859Q")
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The “relevant provisions” are— section 114 (register of members); section 228 (directors' service contracts); section 237 (directors' indemnities); section 358 (records of resolutions etc); section 702; section 720; section 743; section 805; section 809; section 859Q" (a definition handed to a list, the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16228 | (6) A requirement under a relevant provision to keep company records available for inspection is not complied with by keeping them available for inspection at a place specified in the regulations unless all the company's records subject to the requirement are kept there.
@ref s 1136(6) All the records must be kept at the specified place (src:16228)
GIVEN `the place is one specified in the regulations under s 1136` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the company's records subject to the requirement are kept at that place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1136(6) keeping the records available for inspection at the place complies with the requirement` MEANS
    IF NOT `the place is one specified in the regulations under s 1136`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by keeping them available for inspection at a place specified in the regulations"
    ELSE IF NOT `all the company's records subject to the requirement are kept at that place`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not complied with by keeping them available for inspection at a place specified in the regulations unless all the company's records subject to the requirement are kept there"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless" states a necessary condition only; the regulations made under s 1136(1) and (4) decide the rest

-- ---- s 1137: Regulations about inspection of records and provision of copies ---------------------------
-- s 1137(1), (3), (4) and (6): a regulation-making power and its procedure: inert, reason 2.

DECLARE `s 1137 obligation regulated` IS ONE OF
    `s 1137 keeping company records available for inspection`
    `s 1137 providing copies of company records`

DECLARE `s 1137 treatment` IS ONE OF
    `s 1137 treated as having refused inspection`
    `s 1137 treated as having failed to provide a copy`

-- src:16234 | (2) A company that fails to comply with the regulations is treated as having refused inspection or, as the case may be, having failed to provide a copy.
@ref s 1137(2) A company that fails to comply with the regulations is treated as having refused inspection or failed to provide a copy (src:16234)
GIVEN obligation IS A `s 1137 obligation regulated`
      `the company fails to comply with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1137 treatment`
`s 1137(2) the company is treated as having refused or failed` MEANS
    IF `the company fails to comply with the regulations`
    THEN CONSIDER obligation
         WHEN `s 1137 keeping company records available for inspection` THEN JUST `s 1137 treated as having refused inspection`
         WHEN `s 1137 providing copies of company records` THEN JUST `s 1137 treated as having failed to provide a copy`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that fails to comply with the regulations is treated as"

-- src:16239 | (5) Nothing in any provision of this Act or in the regulations shall be read as preventing a company—
-- src:16240 | (a) from affording more extensive facilities than are required by the regulations, or
-- src:16241 | (b) where a fee may be charged, from charging a lesser fee than that prescribed or none at all.
@ref s 1137(5) A company may afford more extensive facilities, or charge a lesser fee (src:16239-16241)
GIVEN `the facilities afforded are more extensive than the regulations require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1137(5)(a) the company is prevented from affording more extensive facilities than the regulations require` MEANS
    IF `the facilities afforded are more extensive than the regulations require`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in any provision of this Act or in the regulations shall be read as preventing a company— (a) from affording more extensive facilities than are required by the regulations"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the flat negative reaches only facilities more extensive than the regulations require

-- src:16239 | (5) Nothing in any provision of this Act or in the regulations shall be read as preventing a company—
-- src:16240 | (a) from affording more extensive facilities than are required by the regulations, or
-- src:16241 | (b) where a fee may be charged, from charging a lesser fee than that prescribed or none at all.
@ref s 1137(5) A company may afford more extensive facilities, or charge a lesser fee (src:16239-16241)
GIVEN `a fee may be charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee charged is lesser than the prescribed fee, or none at all` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1137(5)(b) the company is prevented from charging a lesser fee or none at all` MEANS
    IF `a fee may be charged` AND `the fee charged is lesser than the prescribed fee, or none at all`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in any provision of this Act or in the regulations shall be read as preventing a company— (b) where a fee may be charged, from charging a lesser fee than that prescribed or none at all"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where a fee may be charged, from charging a lesser fee than that prescribed or none at all"

-- ---- s 1138: Duty to take precautions against falsification ---------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1138 kind of company record` IS ONE OF
    `s 1138 a copy of a director's service contract or a memorandum of its terms (s 228)`
    `s 1138 a qualifying indemnity provision (s 237)`
    `s 1138 another company record`

-- src:16249 | (4) This section does not apply to the documents required to be kept under—
-- src:16250 | (a) section 228 (copy of director's service contract or memorandum of its terms); or
-- src:16251 | (b) section 237 (qualifying indemnity provision).
@ref s 1138(4) The section does not apply to the documents kept under s 228 or s 237 (src:16249-16251)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1138 kind of company record`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1138(4) this section applies to the company record` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1138 a copy of a director's service contract or a memorandum of its terms (s 228)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to the documents required to be kept under— (a) section 228"
    WHEN `s 1138 a qualifying indemnity provision (s 237)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to the documents required to be kept under— (b) section 237"
    WHEN `s 1138 another company record` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (4) names only the s 228 and s 237 documents; subsection (1) decides the rest

-- src:16243 | 1138 Duty to take precautions against falsification
-- src:16244 | (1) Where company records are kept otherwise than in bound books, adequate precautions must be taken—
-- src:16245 | (a) to guard against falsification, and
-- src:16246 | (b) to facilitate the discovery of falsification.
@ref s 1138(1) Precautions against falsification where records are kept otherwise than in bound books (src:16243-16246)
GIVEN `the company records are kept otherwise than in bound books` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1138(1) the duty to take precautions applies to the records` MEANS
    IF `the company records are kept otherwise than in bound books`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where company records are kept otherwise than in bound books" (a "where" that fails: the 2026-11-05 ruling)

-- src:16243 | 1138 Duty to take precautions against falsification
-- src:16244 | (1) Where company records are kept otherwise than in bound books, adequate precautions must be taken—
-- src:16245 | (a) to guard against falsification, and
-- src:16246 | (b) to facilitate the discovery of falsification.
@ref s 1138(1) Precautions against falsification where records are kept otherwise than in bound books (src:16243-16246)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1138 kind of company record`
      `the company records are kept otherwise than in bound books` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adequate precautions are taken to guard against falsification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adequate precautions are taken to facilitate the discovery of falsification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1138 the company has complied with this section` MEANS
    IF `s 1138(4) this section applies to the company record` kind EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST TRUE -- the section does not apply to this record, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
    ELSE IF NOT `the company records are kept otherwise than in bound books`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- the duty does not engage, so nothing is left to fail (fork F5)
         ELSE IF `adequate precautions are taken to guard against falsification` AND `adequate precautions are taken to facilitate the discovery of falsification`
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "adequate precautions must be taken— (a) to guard against falsification, and (b) to facilitate the discovery of falsification" (a bare "must" not done: decided at this site, fork F5)

-- src:16247 | (2) If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1138(2) Offence of failing to comply with s 1138 (src:16247)
GIVEN `s 1138 the company has complied with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1138(2) an officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1138 the company has complied with this section`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company fails to comply with this section, an offence is committed" (an "if" that is not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company complied is not known
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is the answer of s 1121

-- src:16248 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1138(3) Penalty for an offence under s 1138 (src:16248)
GIVEN guilty IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1138(3) the penalty for an offence under s 1138` MEANS
    CONSIDER guilty
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                           `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                           `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
                           `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
                           `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is guilty is not known

-- ---- The duties as regulative rules (s 1135(2) and s 1138(1)) -------------------------------------------
-- The text names the company as the party and states no time limit and no consequence beyond the offence of
-- subsection (3) / (2), so the rules carry no WITHIN, and a missed duty is a BREACH with the reason. They are run
-- with #TRACE in coa25-tests-records.l4. A DEONTIC value cannot be compared with EQUALS on the stable binary, so the
-- decision functions above are the asserted twins of these rules.

DECLARE `s 1135 act of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 1135 keep the electronic records capable of being reproduced in hard copy form`
    `s 1138 take adequate precautions against falsification of the records`

-- src:16201 | (2) Where the records are kept in electronic form, they must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form.
@ref s 1135(2) Electronic records must be capable of being reproduced in hard copy form (src:16201)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1135 act of the company`
`s 1135(2) the company must keep electronic records capable of reproduction in hard copy form` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 1135 keep the electronic records capable of being reproduced in hard copy form`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 1135(2): the electronic records are not capable of being reproduced in hard copy form"

-- src:16243 | 1138 Duty to take precautions against falsification
-- src:16244 | (1) Where company records are kept otherwise than in bound books, adequate precautions must be taken—
-- src:16245 | (a) to guard against falsification, and
-- src:16246 | (b) to facilitate the discovery of falsification.
@ref s 1138(1) Precautions against falsification where records are kept otherwise than in bound books (src:16243-16246)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1135 act of the company`
`s 1138(1) the company must take adequate precautions against falsification` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 1138 take adequate precautions against falsification of the records`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 1138(1): adequate precautions were not taken to guard against falsification and to facilitate its discovery"
